  "method": [
    "Read all ten module teaching sequences and their project contracts, failure/acceptance/hint sections; checked original taxonomy objective fit.",
    "Checked exact assigned locator membership and five-category budgets with canonical structural validator; no local/cycle errors.",
    "Inspected and ran the integration verifier: seven fixture expected objects independently recomputed, zero failures.",
    "Hand-checked representative Q7, FIR/IIR, rollover, resource, response-time, roofline, MC/DC and publication-model arithmetic.",
    "Reviewed host/emulator/physical, bounded/unbounded, numeric/physical and logical/OS enforcement distinctions.",
    "Fresh reread of all reported fixes, including the corrected MC/DC hint and new combined absolute/relative tolerance rule with units/reference-uncertainty limits.",
    "Complete saved embedded oracle inspected and executed: 59 fixtures/59 checks, zero failures; integration oracle re-executed: 7 fixtures, zero failures.",
    "Seven independently specified boundary/counterexample probes passed without using fixture expected objects."
  ],
  "structural_errors": [],
  "findings": [
    {
      "id": "EIR-01",
      "severity": "medium",
      "blocking": false,
      "status": "resolved",
      "paths": [
        "curriculum/projects/PR-T35-02.md",
        "curriculum/modules/T35.md"
      ],
      "problem": "Actual denied-effect acceptance is required, but the concrete activity specifies only a private working directory, descriptor inheritance and logical capability membership. Those do not define which attempted OS effect is enforced as denied or how. The prose correctly denies that an ordinary subprocess is automatically a sandbox, but the required activity still lacks the enforcement step.",
      "required_change": "Name a narrow nonprivileged enforced boundary and its negative control. For example, inherit a read-only log descriptor and verify an attempted write fails under the actual OS contract, while explicitly reporting remaining filesystem/process authority. Distinguish that descriptor property and process-memory isolation from a general sandbox. If broader sandboxing is required, inspect and specify its complete selected OS mechanism.",
      "originally_blocking": true,
      "resolution": "Freshly read PR-T35-02 and T35.05/.08: actual inherited O_RDONLY descriptor read, write=-1/EBADF and unchanged digest; separate logical write-config denial and explicit residual filesystem/network/process authority table. No complete sandbox claim."
    },
    {
      "id": "EIR-02",
      "severity": "medium",
      "blocking": false,
      "status": "resolved",
      "paths": [
        "curriculum/projects/PR-T34-06.md"
      ],
      "problem": "The whole project is marked Profile E while its steps ask for -fprofile-generate/-fprofile-use and physical target deployment without identifying where profile collection runs or which instrumentation/runtime/transport services exist. This conflates a hosted PGO comparison with the firmware dependency boundary.",
      "required_change": "Separate hosted PGO collection/comparison, with instrumentation/libgcov dependencies audited, from two independently audited Profile E firmware variants. Reuse prior kernels and describe the two environment boundaries so the eight-hour milestone remains plausible. A bare-metal PGO path instead requires an inspected support/transport contract.",
      "originally_blocking": true,
      "resolution": "Freshly read PR-T34-06: hosted Profile A libgcov/instrumentation/training and held-out comparison explicitly separated from plain/LTO uninstrumented Profile E firmware; independent physical timing and dependency evidence remain required."
    },
    {
      "id": "EIR-03",
      "severity": "low",
      "blocking": false,
      "status": "resolved",
      "paths": [
        "curriculum/projects/PR-T35-01.md",
        "curriculum/projects/PR-T35-03.md",
        "curriculum/projects/PR-T32-06.md",
        "curriculum/modules/T17.md"
      ],
      "problem": "Several project sentences concatenate words and numbers, such as opcode/count descriptions, work-quota contracts and MC/DC pair hints. The T17 project-list preview truncates the FIR/IIR contract at y[n]=0. The detailed project supplies the full recurrence, so this is presentation rather than a numerical failure.",
      "required_change": "Restore spaces in the public authored prose and use complete project-list summaries; preserve identifiers, hex values and equations.",
      "originally_blocking": false,
      "resolution": "Freshly read corrected command/quota contracts, spaced MC/DC pair hint and complete FIR/IIR project-list summary. No arithmetic change hidden in the prose repairs."
    },
    {
      "id": "EIR-04",
      "severity": "low",
      "blocking": false,
      "status": "resolved",
      "paths": [
        "curriculum/guides/integrations.md"
      ],
      "problem": "The P4 activity explicitly consumes P3 output framing, but the integration-family foundation table omits P3 from P4 foundations. The project contract makes the dependency discoverable, yet the table can mislead route planning.",
      "required_change": "List P3 as a P4 foundation or explicitly explain the independently completed shared framing prerequisite.",
      "originally_blocking": false,
      "resolution": "Freshly read integration guide: P4 foundations now explicitly include P3, matching the existing framing-consuming activity."
    }
  ],
  "positive_findings": [
    "Actual F439 hardware closure is never replaced by MPS2 or host model evidence.",
    "DMA cancellation/confirmed stop, CCM reachability and cacheless-core boundaries are explicit.",
    "CBMC unwind, WP assumptions/unsupported goals and sequential Eva limits are disclosed.",
    "Independent mathematical references and fixed numerical contracts precede optimization.",
    "All twenty integration briefs are bounded reuse milestones; their 160 implementation/verification hours are counted once.",
    "Profiles/inventory resolve C17 declared-byte-array/effective-type limits and prohibit delegating studied mechanisms to libc."
  ],
